  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A preparation list shows each requested book, its reader, and its agreed pickup window.\", \"decision\": \"Who should choose when a requested book is prepared?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nHelpers prepare the requested books in one early pass, and staff use the preparation list to group them by pickup window. The desk avoids repeated preparation during the afternoon rush.\nReaders confirm they are on their way, and staff then prepare the requested books from the preparation list. Preparation effort follows readers who are likely to collect soon.\nStaff prepare each requested book shortly before its pickup window, following the preparation list. Shelf space remains available for books whose readers are arriving soon."
    }
